<Simple lang="en" title="Terms of use" description="Terms of use of The Meowpany website.">
  <p>Prices on this site are list prices in US dollars. The price of each project is fixed in a written proposal and contract.</p>
  <p>The quote form estimate is indicative and is not a binding offer.</p>
  <h2>First version with no payment up front</h2>
  <p>After the first call we agree in writing on what the first working version includes, and we deliver it within 72 hours of that agreement. It is not charged and no payment method is requested for it. If the client does not continue, they have no obligation; if they do, the project is governed by the proposal and contract signed by both parties. We build one first version per client and project.</p>
  <h2>Warranty</h2>
  <p>For 60 days after go-live we fix, at no cost, defects in what we delivered, meaning anything that does not work as the approved scope says. It does not cover scope changes, new features or failures caused by third parties (hosting, payment gateways or other services). The contract sets the final conditions of each project.</p>
  <h2>Code ownership</h2>
  <p>What is built specifically for each client belongs to the client once the project is paid. When a project includes modules from The Meowpany's library, the client receives their source code and a perpetual licence, at no extra cost, to use, change and maintain them with whoever they choose; The Meowpany keeps ownership of those modules and may keep using them in other projects. Each project's contract sets the final conditions.</p>
  <h2>Brand</h2>
  <p>The content, logo and The Meowpany brand belong to the company and may not be used without permission.</p>
</Simple>
